  "id": "optimal-foraging-theory",
  "term": "optimal foraging theory",
  "definition": "Optimal foraging theory is the idea that an organism’s food or host choices tend to match what gives it the greatest fitness benefit. In the source packet, it is used to mean that preference should favor the option that leads to better survival, reproduction, or energy-related outcomes.",
